    "https://ap.washington.edu/ahr/position-details/?job_id=188077": {
      "title": "Research Associate Professor, Department of Microbiology",
      "description": "Position Details - Academic Personnel & Faculty Skip to content All the UW Current site Search scope All the UW Current site Enter search text University of Washington University of Washington UW HR Workday Employee Help UW Finance Faculty Senate Menu Home About us About Us Our Strategic Plan Leadership Team Office and Team Contacts Faculty Affairs Advisory Committee News News eDigest Archive For Academic Personnel For Academic Personnel & Faculty New Faculty @UW Faculty Development Faculty Inclusive Excellence ADVANCE Center for Institutional Change Faculty Review Resources Faculty Promotion & Tenure Librarian Reappointment & Promotion Academic Responsibilities Voting Guidelines Time Off and Leaves Postdoctoral Scholars Affairs & Operations Academic Personnel & Faculty Affairs Academic Titles and Ranks Resources Forms and Templates Policies and Procedures Appointment Actions Visas Academic Jobs Academic Personnel & Faculty Academic Personnel & Faculty Academic Personnel & Faculty Affairs Position Details Position Details Research Associate Professor, Department of Microbiology Position Overview School / Campus / College: School of Medicine Organization: Microbiology Title: Research Associate Professor, Department of Microbiology Position Details Position Description The Department of Microbiology at the University of Washington in Seattle is conducting a search for a Research Associate Professor to conduct research focused on retrovirology and cancer biology, with particular emphasis on transmissible cancers. The successful candidate will join a vibrant and collaborative research community and will have opportunities to interact with University of Washington investigators studying microbial pathogenesis, host-microbe interactions, and the development of innovative antimicrobial strategies. We particularly encourage applicants whose work integrates genetic, biochemical, and/or systems-level approaches to understand how transmissible cancers form and transmit, and how they affect their hosts. The position is a 12-month, full-time, non-tenure track appointment in the School of Medicine. The anticipated start date is winter 2026. The base full-time equivalent salary range for this position will be $160,000–$163,000 per annum ($13,333–$13,583 monthly), commensurate with experience and qualifications, or as mandated by a U.S. Department of Labor prevailing wage determination. The successful candidate is expected to lead innovative and impactful research and to contribute to advancing our understanding of fundamental processes related to transmissible cancers, including their detection, transmission, maintenance and treatment, especially in bivalves. We seek applicants who demonstrate commitment to excellence in research and service in a diverse and inclusive academic community. University of Washington faculty engage in teaching, research, and service. Qualifications Applicants must have a strong record of research accomplishments, including 1 year of postdoctoral or independent research experience and a record of peer-reviewed publications. Candidates for this position must hold a PhD degree in microbiology or related discipline (or foreign equivalent). An MD or foreign equivalent is also acceptable. Instructions Applicants should submit the following through Interfolio: A cover letter A curriculum vitae A concise summary of research accomplishments Applicants should arrange for three confidential letters of reference. Recommenders will receive separate instructions automatically through Interfolio. Applications received by September 1, 2026, will receive priority consideration. The position will remain open until filled. Applicants should describe how their past experiences and/or future plans in research, teaching, mentoring, patient care, and/or service will contribute to a welcoming and inclusive academic environment. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Equal Opportunity The University of Washington is committed to fostering an inclusive, respectful and welcoming community for all. As an equal opportunity employer, the University considers applicants for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, national origin, citizenship, sex, pregnancy, age, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, disability, or veteran status consistent with UW Executive Order No. 81 . Benefits Information The University is committed to providing excellent benefits to our faculty. For a summary of available benefits, please see UWHR benefits information . Privacy Notice Your application materials may be used for employment consideration and shared in accordance with UW’s Privacy Policy. Disability Services The University of Washington is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Disability Services Office at 206-543-6450 or dso@uw.edu. Apply now The University of Washington is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier account and can send all application materials, including confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. For help signing up, accessing your account, or submitting your application, please check out Interfolio's help and support section or get in touch via email at help@interfolio.com or phone at (877)997-8807. Title IX Notice The University of Washington does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits sex discrimination and sex-based harassment in its education programs and activities, including in admission and employment. Refer to the UW policies page on the Title IX website to review (1) the University’s policies prohibiting sex- and gender-based violence, harassment, and discrimination and (2) the related procedures for addressing complaints. Inquiries about Title IX may be referred to the University’s Title IX Coordinator , the U.S. Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights , or both. To report information or make a complaint about conduct that may constitute sex discrimination or sex-based harassment, submit an online Title IX report or email or call the Office of the Title IX Coordinator. Office of the Title IX Coordinator Valery Richardson, Title IX Coordinator 4311 11th Ave NE Seattle, WA 98105 206-221-7932 TitleIX@uw.edu ← Back to all positions University of Washington Be boundless Connect with us: Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Pinterest Accessibility Contact Us Jobs Campus Safety My UW Rules Docket Privacy Terms Newsletter © 2026 University of Washington  |  Seattle, WA"
